+### Explicitly checked and found healthy (no action)
+
+- **Golden discipline**: `FMeleeMathConstants` + the T2.1 golden naming every literal is exactly how
+  placeholders should be locked; the arc-band mid-bucket errata (bucket-START -> MID-BUCKET) is
+  correctly implemented in `SectorCenterDeg` and pinned by the round-trip assertions.
+- **Determinism posture**: seed-derived worker rolls (no wall-clock, per-pair `RollCount` input),
+  sorted-key iteration everywhere, `GetSortedEngagementKeys` with full tie-breaks -- consistent.
+- **Redundant-test scan**: no duplicated coverage found across the 11 unit test files
+  (RecordLifecycle/OrderAttack/SaveRoundTrip/HashTerms/HitChanceGolden/BudgetCoverage/TallyAssign/
+  SpatialHash/ClusterRecords are disjoint; the garrison suite doesn't re-test combat). The only
+  redundancy was the superseded perf stub (C-6) and the dead seam golden (A-3).
+- **Flags-off identity**: every combat gate reads game-thread-only at top-of-Execute and returns
+  before touching state; the demo session-on flips are confined to the demo map's game mode.
+- **`RingRadiusFor` reach-class clamp** (`FMath::Min<uint8>(Seeker.ReachClass, 7)`) is repeated
+  consistently at each of the three reach-table consumers -- the table is 8 wide and the enum has 5
+  values, so the clamp is the correct guard; B-1's shared helper keeps it in one place.
